.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-cf-evaluate 1  "rev-stealth-cf-evaluate " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-cf\-evaluate \- Defender\-testbed evaluation of Cloudflare Turnstile resilience
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth cf\-evaluate\fR [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] <\fB\-\-url\fR> [\fB\-\-session\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-i\-have\-authorization\fR] [\fB\-\-obscura\fR] [\fB\-\-require\-vpn\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-no\-vpn\fR] [\fB\-\-vpn\-instance\fR] [\fB\-\-proxy\-tier\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-fallback\fR] [\fB\-\-leak\-poll\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-use\-auth\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-domain\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Defender\-testbed evaluation of Cloudflare Turnstile resilience. Launches the stealth browser against \-\-url and records the Turnstile challenge trajectory without invoking any solver. Requires explicit AUP authorization.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR
Output format for this subcommand: `human` (default) or `json`. Shadows the global `\-\-format` for this invocation. Same value enum as the global flag; the JSON output is documented under `docs/json\-schemas/cli/<subcommand>.output.json`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-session\-id\fR \fI<SESSION_ID>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-i\-have\-authorization\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-obscura\fR \fI<OBSCURA>\fR

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBREV_STEALTH_OBSCURA\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-vpn\fR
Phase 6c: fail\-closed VPN\-required guard. See spider \-\-require\-vpn
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-no\-vpn\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-vpn\-instance\fR \fI<VPN_INSTANCE>\fR
Phase 6d: force a specific VPN instance from the configured pool
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-tier\fR \fI<PROXY_TIER>\fR
Force a named proxy tier (e.g. "direct", "surfshark", "warp", "iproyal") or "auto" to use the configured fallback chain. Mutually exclusive with `\-\-vpn\-instance` unless the tier is exactly "surfshark"
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-fallback\fR
Disable the fallback chain; one attempt at the selected tier only
.TP
\fB\-\-leak\-poll\-secs\fR \fI<LEAK_POLL_SECS>\fR [default: 30]
Phase 6e: background leak monitor poll interval (seconds)
.TP
\fB\-\-use\-auth\fR \fI<USE_AUTH>\fR
Replay stored auth cookies and browser headers from the named profile
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-domain\fR \fI<AUTH_DOMAIN>\fR
Auth AAD/domain context to load; defaults to the target host
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth cf\-evaluate \-\-url https://example.com \-\-i\-have\-authorization
  $ rev\-stealth cf\-evaluate \-\-url https://x.test \-\-i\-have\-authorization \-\-use\-auth my\-profile
  $ rev\-stealth cf\-evaluate \-\-url https://x.test \-\-i\-have\-authorization \-\-require\-vpn

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Evaluation completed.
  1  UserError        Bad \-\-url / AUP rejection / config error.
  2  TransientError   Browser / network transient failure.
  3  PermanentError   Obscura missing or evaluation unsupported.

ENV:
  REV_STEALTH_OBSCURA       Override the obscura binary path.
  REV_SCRAPING_REQUIRE_VPN  When `1`, enforces VPN\-required guard.
